course: dictionary
lesson: 11752
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them tell you which one is meant. This is called context. Banger is one of these words. It can mean a sausage, a firework, an old car, or a great song.
explain: «Mum made bangers and mash for tea.» Mash is potato, so a banger here must be a sausage. «Be careful, a banger can hurt your fingers, so only an adult should light it.» Lighting and hurting point to a firework.
explain: «Grandad's old banger rattled up the hill.» Old and rattled tell you it is a car in bad condition. «This new song is an absolute banger!» New and absolute, with the word song, show that it means a really good, exciting song.
fact: A banger can mean a sausage, especially in the UK, and bangers and mash is a classic meal.
fact: A banger can also mean a firework that makes a loud bang.
fact: In informal speech, a banger can mean an old car in bad condition that often makes noises.
fact: In slang, a banger is a really good, exciting song, usually loud and catchy.
exercise: «Mum made bangers and mash for tea.» What is a banger in this sentence? | *A sausage | An old car | A loud song | A firework
exercise: «Be careful, a banger can hurt your fingers, so only an adult should light it.» What does banger mean here? | A sausage for tea | *A firework that makes a loud bang | A cheap, rattling car | A great, catchy song
exercise: «Grandad's old banger rattled up the hill.» Which word is the best clue that banger means a car? | Grandad's | *rattled | banger | the
test: «This new song is an absolute banger!» What does banger mean here? | A firework | An old car in bad condition | A sausage | *A really good, catchy song
test: «The banger went off with a huge bang on Bonfire Night.» What does banger mean? | A quiet song | An old, rattling car | A sausage for supper | *A firework
exam: Which meaning fits this sentence? «The dog ate a banger from the barbecue.» | A great song | An old car | *A sausage | A firework
